    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm doing some planning for a cedar deck build in vancouver. i need to walk through the basics of calculating live load vs dead load for the beam and post sizing. can u explain the difference and how they factor into the total load? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In deck building, Live Load (LL) and Dead Load (DD) are two types of loads that need to be considered. Dead Load refers to the weight of the physical elements of the deck itself, such as the joists, decking boards, railings, and post footings. Live Load, on the other hand, is the weight of the people, furniture, and other temporary fixtures that will be placed on the deck. When calculating beam and post sizes, you'll need to factor in both Dead Load and Live Load, but typically, Live Load has a higher impact and is usually considered first.",
      "source": "target",
